        {
          "ruleId": "data_exfil-006",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "## Description\nLack of detailed error handling that could lead to information disclosure. The application provides minimal error responses (just 404 status) without proper error sanitization. While this specific case is not verbose, the lack of comprehensive error handling framework means errors elsewhere in the application could potentially leak sensitive information.\n\n## Impact\nIf database errors or other exceptions occur, they might be exposed to clients with sensitive information about the internal system structure, file paths, or database schema.\n\n## Recommendations\n1. Implement a centralized error handling mechanism that sanitizes all error responses. 2. Log detailed errors server-side but return generic error messages to clients. 3. Implement proper exception handling throughout the application. 4. Use structured logging that separates internal debugging information from client responses.",
            "markdown": "## Description\nLack of detailed error handling that could lead to information disclosure. The application provides minimal error responses (just 404 status) without proper error sanitization. While this specific case is not verbose, the lack of comprehensive error handling framework means errors elsewhere in the application could potentially leak sensitive information.\n\n## Impact\nIf database errors or other exceptions occur, they might be exposed to clients with sensitive information about the internal system structure, file paths, or database schema.\n\n## Recommendations\n1. Implement a centralized error handling mechanism that sanitizes all error responses. 2. Log detailed errors server-side but return generic error messages to clients. 3. Implement proper exception handling throughout the application. 4. Use structured logging that separates internal debugging information from client responses."
          },
